  data: {
    LLM: "Dump your high-value Spades! If you have the Queen of Spades, you MUST try to discard it when someone else leads a high Spade (Ace or King). If you don't have the Queen, avoid leading Spades until you know who has it.\n\nSuit Exhaustion: Choose one suit where you have very few cards (e.g., only one Heart). Void that suit early by playing your card when you can. Once you are void, you have a safe 'dumping ground' for the Queen of Spades or high Tens when those suits are led.\n\nThe Ace Shield: If you hold a high Ace, don't lead that suit early. Save it for the end of the game when others are more likely to have discarded their low cards, forcing you to win multiple high-point cards at once. Track which point cards have been playedâ€”if the Queen hasn't appeared yet and you're holding the King of Spades, be very careful about leading Spades.",
    Player: "Dump your high-value Spades! If you have the Queen of Spades, you MUST try to discard it when someone else leads a high Spade (Ace or King). If you don't have the Queen, avoid leading Spades until you know who has it.\n\nSuit Exhaustion: Choose one suit where you have very few cards (e.g., only one Heart). Void that suit early by playing your card when you can. Once you are void, you have a safe 'dumping ground' for the Queen of Spades or high Tens when those suits are led.\n\nThe Ace Shield: If you hold a high Ace, don't lead that suit early. Save it for the end of the game when others are more likely to have discarded their low cards, forcing you to win multiple high-point cards at once. Track which point cards have been playedâ€”if the Queen hasn't appeared yet and you're holding the King of Spades, be very careful about leading Spades.",
